A||||3||Seanh||Removing Headbolts!?!||||8||
Z||000000||Seanh||12-10-2000||06:18 PM||||I am trying to take the heads off the 305 engine and I cant do it! I admit I am not the strongest person in the world, but they will not come off for me or my dad. We were just using a heavy-dudy rachet set. How should I get them off. I dont want to risk breaking them off in case I decide to use this engine in a future project. I was afraid I might break them if I use a 90 Degree attachment and a larger breaker bar? Anything else I should know?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-10-2000||08:48 PM||||All I can suggest is lots of penetrating oil, liquid wrench or WD-40.  Keep putting it on, never hurts to put too much on.  I dont think heating it would be a good idea, you dont want to warp it.  Breaker bar could work, you can get a lot of force through one of those, so be careful!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||12-10-2000||10:21 PM||||I second the use of copious amounts of lube.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Keep on spraying and waiting and spraying. If you have an impact socket you could try using that in quick bursts. If not, your only option is a larger bar, but when it starts turning, keep putting lube in there. Make sure the socket is the RIGHT size... Don't say "close enough".||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||12-10-2000||10:32 PM||||Use a breaker bar and a cheater pipe. Don't worry, they won't break. 305's are commonly torqued in at 90 ft. lbs. and with the combination of the sealer, they're pretty #@$! tight!||||reg||1
